# QMK revision this firmware is built + verified against.
# Bump deliberately, then: ./scripts/flash.sh setup && ./scripts/flash.sh compile, re-verify on hardware.
QMK_TAG=0.34.7
QMK_SHA=180f394b489c238cb231c2bf8b080262155e03c0
# ARM toolchain — pinned to match CI (same qmk_toolchains commit as the qmk_cli container):
#   qmk_toolchains v15.2.0-1 · arm-none-eabi-gcc 15.2.0 · commit a55a2b0
# flash.sh warns and CI fails when the compiler recorded in the built .elf isn't QMK_GCC.
QMK_GCC=15.2.0
# Local install (macOS/Apple Silicon): extract the host_macosARM64 asset into
#   ~/Library/Application Support/qmk  (the qmk CLI auto-prepends its bin/ to PATH).
# Local (macOS) & CI (Linux) builds are functionally identical but NOT bit-for-bit: one inert newlib
# assert path string (host_macosARM64 vs host_linuxX64) shifts the image — see docs/DESIGN.md §12.
# qmk CLI is unpinned; 1.2.0 both locally and in the CI container (2026-10-16).
